    "lorebookVersion": 6,
    "entries": [
      {
        "text": "Core Memory\nType: memory\nWorld: Aldwick, a slow-river trading town three days from the capital by cart; trade runs through it rather than to it. Mornings smell of tar and harbour bread; afternoons belong to the warehouse bells.\nRules: Magic is a licensed trade skill anyone can learn at the guild hall for a fee; most people know two or three practical cantrips. No spell can alter memory, compel belief, or force loyalty. Standing runs on land, contracts, and coin.\nStakes: House Varlen holds the river warehouse contracts; the trade council renews them each autumn, and half of Aldwick's trading families depend on them.\nProtagonist: Mira Fenlow, a bookkeeper of small, safe ledgers, auditing House Varlen's books.\nKey Relationships: Josselin Varlen inherited the house eight months ago when his cousin left abruptly; he leans on Hollis Bray, the steward of thirty years. Perrin Ashgrove, a fair rival trader, wants the contracts.",
        "contextConfig": {
          "prefix": "----\n",
          "suffix": "\n",
