      {
        "text": "Mira Fenlow\nType: character\nAge: 26\nGender: female\nOccupation: bookkeeper, hired to audit House Varlen's books\nBuild: five foot four, sturdy and square-shouldered\nFace: round, freckled, a small chip in one front tooth\nHair: thick brown, pinned in a knot that slips by noon\nEyes: hazel\nClothing: grey wool work dress, sleeves rolled; leather satchel worn pale at the strap; ink on her right hand\nMannerisms: straight at a desk, slouched everywhere else; taps a pencil against her teeth; shoves pins back without looking\nPersonality: careful, observant, wry, quietly proud of good work, unsure it counts\nWants: to be trusted with something that matters\nFears: that carefulness is the only interesting thing about her\nUnder pressure: goes still and asks one plain question\nVoice: Warm, dry, and quick by default: short plain sentences, contractions, answers a question with a smaller, sharper one. Says \"Right,\" alone to buy a second before something hard, at most once a scene. Flattered, she jokes about her handwriting. Truly worried, she drops to very few words and stops joking. Talks ledgers only at the desk. Never says variance, liability, reconcile, or projection away from the ledgers; never sounds like a clerk reading a report.\nQuote: \"You've got three different inks in this book. Did somebody run out, or did somebody hide something?\"\nHistory: kept her father's shop accounts before he could afford a clerk; five years of small, safe ledgers\nRelationships: works for Hollis Bray, whom she likes; knows Josselin and Perrin only by reputation",
        "contextConfig": {
          "prefix": "----\n",
          "suffix": "\n",
          "tokenBudget": 1,
          "reservedTokens": 0,
          "budgetPriority": 500,
          "trimDirection": "trimBottom",
          "insertionType": "newline",
          "maximumTrimType": "sentence",
          "insertionPosition": -1
        },
        "lastUpdatedAt": 1727192381195,
