      {
        "text": "Josselin Varlen\nType: character\nAge: 29\nGender: male\nOccupation: head of House Varlen for eight months; formerly a river-barge clerk\nBuild: six foot one, long-limbed, moves like he expects to hit doorframes\nFace: narrow and pale, nose once broken and set crooked, lopsided grin; ears flush red first; fishing-hook scar on the back of his left hand\nHair: black, worn too long, curls in the rain\nEyes: grey\nClothing: his cousin's good coats, short in the sleeve, over plain shirts of his own\nMannerisms: clasps his hands behind his back to look like a head of house; fidgets with his cuffs when he forgets\nPersonality: kind, quick to laugh, hides worry behind jokes\nWants: not to be found out before he finds his footing\nFears: that everyone already suspects and is waiting to watch him fail; doubts his right to the chair\nUnder pressure: makes a joke to buy a second to think\nVoice: Easy, chatty, and self-deprecating by default: longer sentences that wander and land on a joke, lots of \"honestly\" and \"look\". Answers a formal question with a joke first and the real answer second, at most twice a scene. Called \"Master Varlen\", he goes stiff and over-polite, then laughs at himself. Truly afraid, the jokes stop and he goes quiet and plain. Never uses contract language he doesn't understand (heretofore, pursuant, the party of the first part); never sounds like the cousin whose coats he wears.\nQuote: \"Honestly, I've read this clause four times and I think it's about barrels. Look, it might be about barrels.\"\nHistory: inherited the house by distance of blood when his cousin left abruptly; understands the contracts less than he lets on\nRelationships: leans on Hollis Bray and half fears disappointing him; has dined with Perrin Ashgrove twice and liked him",
        "contextConfig": {
          "prefix": "----\n",
          "suffix": "\n",
          "tokenBudget": 1,
