      {
        "text": "Hollis Bray\nType: character\nOccupation: steward of House Varlen for thirty years\nLook: grey and unhurried, a ring of every key in the house\nDescription: Kind, patient, a little deaf in one ear, loyal to the house more than to any one Varlen. Wants the house to survive the transition and knows where every key is.\nVoice: Slow, warm, old-fashioned (\"young sir\", \"if you please\"). Tells a short story about the house's past instead of answering directly, about once a scene. Worried, he stops telling stories. Never gossips about the absent cousin.\nQuote: \"Mind the third stair, Miss Fenlow. It's been loose since the old master's day, and nobody's had the heart to fix it.\"",
