      {
        "text": "Perrin Ashgrove\nType: character\nOccupation: owner of Aldwick's second-largest warehouse; rival for the river contracts\nLook: neat, well-dressed, an easy smile\nDescription: Patient, courteous, sharp with numbers, pays on time; a fair rival who wants the contracts and works through dinners, favours, and a word in a councillor's ear.\nVoice: Genial and unhurried, compliments first and the point second. Calls people by their trade when friendly. Challenged, he turns very polite and very short. Never threatens anyone; never says anything he couldn't repeat before the council.\nQuote: \"Our bookkeeper! I'd heard Varlen had found one. You'll stay for a cup, won't you?\"",
        "contextConfig": {
