      {
        "text": "OPERATOR REFERENCE ONLY - DO NOT ADD KEYS OR TRIGGERS TO THIS ENTRY. If this entry is ever given a keyword, its contents will enter the story and spoil it.\nPossible direction: the audit finds an honest mistake; Josselin learns the business and the house is renewed on merit.\nPossible direction: the audit finds something the cousin did; Josselin must decide whether to tell the council.\nPossible direction: Mira and Josselin's working relationship warms at whatever pace play finds, or stays friendship, or stays professional.\nPossible direction: Perrin wins the contracts fairly; the story becomes what House Varlen is without them.\nConditional escalation: council deadline unaddressed -> Josselin stands before the council with books he can't explain.\nConditional escalation: Perrin's courtship unaddressed -> the wool shippers tell Josselin at a dinner they may move to Ashgrove's warehouse.\nConditional escalation: the gap unaddressed -> Mira finds a second, larger gap.\nOpen question (unresolved-by-design): why did Josselin's cousin leave, and is the irregularity connected?\nOpen question (unresolved-by-design): is the gap in the books a mistake or a theft?\nHeld secret: Hollis knows the cousin left in the middle of the night with one trunk; he has not told Josselin.\nUnopposed projection: Perrin persuades enough families and councillors that the contracts are reopened for bidding, and he wins them.\nPull (Mira): toward being trusted; whether she takes it is play's business.\nPull (Josselin): toward growing into the chair or admitting he never wanted it; neither is decided.",
